{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Woe, she who terrifies</b> — Yefet says: like נוראה. And Rabbi Yeshuʿah says: from the root of סורר ומורה, and the alef is in place of the heh as the root letter, like כעוטיה, where the yod is in place of the heh. And some say: it is like ושמתיך כראי, and remove מראתו." "<b>And she is refined</b> — from the root of לחם מגואל. And Rabbi Moses said: from the language of גאולה, though she polluted [it]; HaShem redeemed, and the meaning applies to Jerusalem. And היונה is from the root of לא תונה, and the active verb exits from the binyan qal like יורה, from the root ירה ויורה. Or one like יונה, seductive in her beauty, like יונתי תמתי."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The examples כראי/מראתו are from Isaiah 62:3 and Proverbs 25:5 respectively, cited by root only without verse references as in the source.", 1 "'She polluted' translates מרתה, reading the resh-ת root; the sentence is compressed and the subject of 'she polluted' is left unspecified in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:25.968497449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}